[0.000, "o", "\u001b[32m✔\u001b[39m \u001b[32mRoot cause isolated.\u001b[39m\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n```markdown\r\n1. **Root Cause**: The breaking change occurred in `user.js` at line 4, introduced in commit `b83c577` (refactored: updated user schema). The `userId` property was renamed to `user_id`.\r\n\r\n2. **Attributed Prompt**: The specific Cursor prompt that likely caused this diff is: \"Rename userId to user_id across the returned profile object.\"\r\n\r\n3. **The Shift**: The code broke due to a schema key rename from `userId` to `user_id`. The `app.js` file is trying to access `profile.userId`, which is now undefined.\r\n\r\n4. **Patch**:\r\n```diff\r\ndiff --git a/app.js b/app.js\r\nindex e951f31..c1f0d91 100644\r\n--- a/app.js\r\n+++ b/app.js\r\n@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@ function renderDashboard() {\r\n   const profile = getUserProfile(\"usr_123\");\r\n   \r\n-  // This line expects `userId`\r\n-  console.log(`Loading dashboard for user ID: ${profile.userId.toUpperCase()}`);\r\n+  console.log(`Loading dashboard for user ID: ${profile.user_id.toUpperCase()}`);\r\n }\r\n```\r\n```\r\n\r\n"]
